The target-owned e2ee test uses Paseo's in-memory transport-pair idea with microtask delivery, explicit event observation and deterministic teardown. It adds ciphertext-tamper and substituted-key checks.

`packages/client/src/e2ee/encrypted-channel.ts` differs from the pinned file by two non-null assertions on line 576, added so the file type-checks under this repository's `noUncheckedIndexedAccess`; they are erased at compile time, so the executable JavaScript is unchanged, and the only possible emitted difference is the file's modification-notice comment at the top of the file, which states the change; `packages/client/src/e2ee/closure.json` records the two assertions and the notice with both hashes.
